# Tailwind className Standards

## Always use `cn` for className composition

Never concatenate or template-literal className strings directly. Always use the `cn` utility (from `@/lib/utils`) to combine classes, even for a single conditional.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<div className={`flex flex-col ${isActive ? "text-emerald-400" : "text-neutral-400"}`} />

// ✅ GOOD
<div className={cn("flex flex-col", isActive ? "text-emerald-400" : "text-neutral-400")} />
```

## Split long className strings across multiple lines

When a className string would exceed ~80 characters, split it into grouped logical chunks inside `cn`. Group by concern: layout, spacing, typography, colour/state.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<a className="flex w-full items-center justify-center gap-1.5 border-t border-neutral-700/60 px-3 py-2.5 text-xs font-medium text-neutral-400 transition-colors hover:text-emerald-400" />

// ✅ GOOD
<a
  className={cn(
    "flex w-full items-center justify-center gap-1.5",
    "border-t border-neutral-700/60 px-3 py-2.5",
    "text-xs font-medium text-neutral-400 transition-colors hover:text-emerald-400",
  )}
/>
```
